  "behavior": [
    "Fixed safe stack byte snapshots preserve Native-tagged geterrmessage, raw seterrmessage including NA and GNU8191byte cap, copied reads before any mutable error-state lend; C setter can read its own original buffer without aliasing.",
    "Own native arguments and original runtime before checks; snapshot before output allocation and constructors; deny canonical getter allocation at original cap1 while fixed state needs zero workspace. GC mutation, panic, revocation and foreign exact-address rejection remain checked.",
    "Canonical simple errors install bare original bytes before every matching handler, including two collecting mutating calling handlers; generic supplied conditions keep prior state.",
    "GNU-derived R try closure uses owned text primitives for message construction and preserves outFile/options/visibility/width/condition attributes. Adapt one caller lookup to native tryCatch frame shape and prevent unadapted upstream staging shadow. Remove native try handler and obsolete guard. Optional memory-profiling reports native four-frame chain around real try closure; default profile allocates no trace-entry metadata.",
    "Share pure safe GNU UTF8 suffix repair between fixed buffer and canonical Diagnostic. Preserve the valid character preceding stray continuation bytes, leave earlier invalid bytes intact; canonical diagnostics repair only when clipped, Rstrncpy always repairs. Validate768oracle rows, every byte after ASCII, two-byte and four-byte prefixes."
  ],
